### 10. Exception Testing Patterns

**MANDATORY exception testing pattern for repository layer:**
```java
@Test
@DisplayName("Find entity should throw DataAccessException when database error occurs")
void testFindEntityDatabaseErrorThrowsDataAccessException() {
    // Given
    Integer entityId = 1;
    String expectedJpql = "SELECT e FROM Entity e WHERE e.id = :id";
    TypedQuery<Entity> mockQuery = mock(TypedQuery.class);
    
    given(this.entityManager.createQuery(expectedJpql, Entity.class)).willReturn(mockQuery);
    given(mockQuery.setParameter("id", entityId)).willReturn(mockQuery);
    given(mockQuery.getSingleResult()).willThrow(new DataAccessException("Database connection failed") {});
    
    // When & Then
    assertThatThrownBy(() -> this.repository.findEntityById(entityId))
        .isInstanceOf(DataAccessException.class)
        .hasMessageContaining("Database connection failed");
        
    then(this.entityManager).should().createQuery(expectedJpql, Entity.class);
    then(mockQuery).should().setParameter("id", entityId);
    then(mockQuery).should().getSingleResult();
}
```

### 11. Transaction Testing

**For @Transactional and @WriterRoute methods, test:**
```java
@Test
@DisplayName("Create entities should use writer route for database operations")
void testCreateEntitiesUsesWriterRouteForDatabaseOperations() {
    // Given
    List<Entity> entities = RepositoryTestDataFactory.createEntityList();
    List<Entity> savedEntities = RepositoryTestDataFactory.createSavedEntityList();
    given(this.jpaRepository.saveAll(entities)).willReturn(savedEntities);
    
