### 26. JOOQ Testing Best Practices - MANDATORY CHECKLIST

#### 26.1 Before Writing JOOQ Tests

**MUST UNDERSTAND:**
- [ ] **JOOQ Table Aliases**: Understand all table aliases used in query (e.g., `var ts = CstTimesheetT.CST_TIMESHEET_T`)
- [ ] **Join Relationships**: Understand all LEFT JOIN and INNER JOIN relationships
- [ ] **Dynamic Conditions**: Understand all conditional query building (if/else, switch statements)
- [ ] **Parameter Usage**: Understand how method parameters affect query construction
- [ ] **Helper Methods**: Identify any helper methods that build parts of the query

#### 26.2 JOOQ Test Coverage Requirements

**MANDATORY test scenarios for JOOQ methods:**
- [ ] **Valid Parameters**: Test with valid parameters that would execute successfully
- [ ] **Null Parameters**: Test with null optional parameters
- [ ] **Invalid Parameters**: Test with invalid parameters (e.g., invalid entity types)
- [ ] **Edge Cases**: Test with empty collections, boundary values
- [ ] **Pagination**: Test different pagination parameters (page 0, page 2, different sizes)
- [ ] **Sorting**: Test with/without sorting parameters (if applicable)
- [ ] **Filtering**: Test with/without filter parameters (if applicable)
- [ ] **Multiple Branches**: Test all conditional branches (e.g., entityType 1 vs 3)

#### 26.3 JOOQ Test Verification Strategy

**What to verify in JOOQ tests:**
- ✅ **Method executes**: Verify the method can be called without syntax errors
- ✅ **Parameter validation**: Verify parameters are used in the method
- ✅ **Conditional logic**: Verify different code paths are executed
- ✅ **Exception handling**: Verify exceptions are handled or propagated appropriately

**What NOT to verify in JOOQ tests:**
- ❌ **SQL generation**: Don't test the actual SQL generated by JOOQ
- ❌ **Query execution**: Don't test if the query actually runs against a database
- ❌ **JOOQ internals**: Don't test JOOQ framework behavior
- ❌ **Result mapping**: Don't test JOOQ's `.into()` mapping (this is framework functionality)

